.TH SDL_HINT_X11_FORCE_OVERRIDE_REDIRECT 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_X11_FORCE_OVERRIDE_REDIRECT \- A variable controlling whether X11 windows are marked as override-redirect.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_X11_FORCE_OVERRIDE_REDIRECT \(dqSDL_X11_FORCE_OVERRIDE_REDIRECT\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If set, this _might_ increase framerate at the expense of the desktop not working as expected\[char46] Override-redirect windows aren\(aqt noticed by the window manager at all\[char46]
.PP
You should probably only use this for fullscreen windows, and you probably shouldn\(aqt even use it for that\[char46] But it\(aqs here if you want to try!
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Do not mark the window as override-redirect\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Mark the window as override-redirect\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before creating a window\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

